go 1.26

// The module lives in go/, so a workspace at the project root is what brings
// its `tool github.com/wailsapp/wails/v3/cmd/wails3` directive into scope for
// `go tool wails3` run from here. Without it the CLI is invisible and the
// build fails with `go: no such tool "wails3"` — which reads like a missing
// install rather than a missing workspace. lthn/desktop has the same file for
// the same reason; this fixture is only faithful with it.
use ./go
